1. Inspect the entire existing repository.
2. Identify the framework, dependencies, routes, components, layouts, database integration, authentication system, API routes, and existing functionality.
3. Identify what is already implemented and what is incomplete.
4. Inspect the current backend/API contracts.
5. Identify existing design decisions and reusable components.
6. Check whether the application already has authentication, role-based access, seed data, and persistent storage.
7. Run the application and inspect existing errors.
8. Prepare an implementation plan based on the actual repository.

